<% content_for :title, "Readme – SageTimer" %>

<div class="tools-page">
  <h1>Readme</h1>

  <section class="tools-section">
    <h2>About SageTimer</h2>
    <div class="tools-content">
      <p>SageTimer is a lane scheduling and timing management application for Championship & Invitational Swim Meets. It helps meet organizers, coaches, officials, and lane timers coordinate lane assignments and bookings.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-section">
    <h2>Features</h2>
    <ul class="tools-list">
      <li>Lane Timer meet schedule dashboard with drag-and-drop booking management</li>
      <li>Lanes 1–10 support A/B sub-lane timers; while Lanes 0 and 11 are backup for the backup timer "lanes", one for each side of the pool</li>
      <li>Club and workout group management with bookings status tracking</li>
      <li>Booking list with sorting, searching, and club filtering</li>
      <li>Role-based access control (Admin, Lane Timer, Head Timer, Official, Meet Management, Coach, and Meet Host (COMSA)</li>
      <li>Tools page with meet information, FAQs, links, and downloadable files</li>
      <li>Meet and session configuration by ADMIN only</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-section">
    <h2>User Roles</h2>
    <ul class="tools-list">
      <li><strong>Lane Timer</strong> — Access to Meet Dashboards, bookings, Team Directory and Tools</li>
      <li><strong>Head Lane Timer</strong> — Access to Meet Dashboards, bookings, Team Directory and Tools</li>
      <li><strong>Official</strong> — View Schedule Dashboards</li>
      <li><strong>Meet Management</strong> — View Schedule Dashboards</li>
      <li><strong>Coach</strong> — Access to edit and confirm the Team Directory Page, as well as to Meet Dashboards and Tools</li>
      <li><strong>COMSA</strong> — View Schedule Dashboards, Post-Meet Analytics (please request a specific LogIn from Hugh Duffy)</li>
      <li><strong>Admin</strong> — Full access to all features including user, meet, and session management (reserved for Hugh and Joshua only), and Post-Meet Analytics</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-section">
    <h2>Getting Started</h2>
    <div class="tools-content">
      <p>Log in with your assigned username and password, or <%= link_to "create a new account", signup_path, style: "color: var(--primary); text-decoration: underline;" %> to get started.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
